{"ticker":"LEAPIND","symbol":"LEAPIND","instrumentId":3203735,"name":"Leap India Ltd","industry":"NSE-Comml Svcs-Leasing","about":"\"LEAP India provides tech-enabled asset pooling and supply-chain solutions, allowing businesses to rent and reuse logistics equipment instead of owning it. Its offerings include pallets, containers, material-handling equipment, returnable packaging, warehousing and asset-management services.\n\nThe company operates across India through 29 warehouses/fulfilment centres and 7 outsourced pallet manufacturing units, supporting more than 10,100 touchpoints. Its pooling model includes asset distribution, tracking, maintenance and reuse.\n\nIts solutions support FMCG, retail, e-commerce, automotive, pharmaceuticals, industrial manufacturing and logistics businesses. The assets facilitate storage, material handling and transportation while reducing capital investment, packaging waste and logistics costs.\"","website":"www.leapindia.net","location":null,"exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:38:01.601Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":129.15,"changePct":-3.806047966631897,"week52High":168.4,"week52Low":0},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹5,690 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹618 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"193,835,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"51"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"125,298,979"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"0.00%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"—"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"1.3"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"117.0%"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"-0.15"},{"label":"Beta","value":"1.56"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"71%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"67.09"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"85–89"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"0.0%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"22.22"},{"label":"Volume","value":"873,854"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"1,989,524"},{"label":"Master score","value":"43"},{"label":"EPS rating","value":"89"}